a Vega chart that:\n- Positions the legend below the chart, and\n- Places the legend entries horizontally, not vertically\n\nI wrote and validated a custom Vega spec using the Vega online editor.\nHowever, when I used the same spec in my project, the legend entries were all placed on top of each other.\nUpon inspection, I found that the `transform` attributes of all `path` element had the same x value: \n\n```\ntransform=\"translate(0,25)\"\n```\n\nwhich obviously wasn't the case with the Vega online editor.\n\nDigging around a little more, I noticed that Vega online editor uses Vega v1.3.3 + D3 v3.2.7, whereas my project uses Vega v1.3.3 + D3 v3.4.3.\n\nAnd I found the following changes in D3 that seems to be causing this issue:\n- https://github.com/mbostock/d3/commit/113032bc977ec1d196280597b060e17083bda90d\n- https://github.com/mbostock/d3/commit/d6ca25e87daf2849b6494051ccab0bd289264088\n\nMore specifically, in my case, `scale(x)` function was returning `NaN`, and Vega in turn was setting it to `0`.\n\nWhen I changed my project to use D3 v3.2.7, the problem disappeared.\n\nIs this a known issue?\n\nI've also created an issue with Vega project just in case:\nhttps://github.com/trifacta/vega/issues/183\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d3/d3/issues/1835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d3/d3/issues/1835/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":128783511,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDEyODc4MzUxMQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/d3/d3/issues/events/128783511","actor":{"login":"bmesuere","id":481872,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTg3Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/481872?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmesuere","html_url":"https://github.com/bmesuere","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmesuere/foll